# Production and shared configuration need platform and security together.

*                       @Mindclade/platform

# Anything under a production path. The ruleset in github-config additionally requires two
# approvals for tier=foundation repositories, so this is the "who", not the "how many".
/5-workloads/production/ @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security
/2-environments/production/ @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Organization-wide: policies, log sinks, KMS, Security Command Center.
/1-org/                 @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Network perimeter. A firewall or VPC-SC change is a security change regardless of which
# environment it lands in.
/3-networks/            @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Admission control and perimeter enforcement.
**/binary-authorization/ @Mindclade/security
**/vpc-sc-perimeter/     @Mindclade/security

# Partner tenancy — isolation boundaries.
/4-projects/partners/ @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Shared config reaches every unit, so a change here is effectively a change everywhere.
/root.hcl               @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security
/account.hcl            @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security
/_envcommon/            @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

/.github/workflows/     @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Browser access controls and activation handoffs
/5-workloads/**/iap-access/ @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security
